<title>INDIA: Bombay bourse declares two brokers defaulters.</title>
<headline>Bombay bourse declares two brokers defaulters.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bombay Stock Exchange (BSE) has declared two of its members defaulters, the Business Standard newspaper said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The net loss suffered by the two brokers is about 20 million rupees after taking into account the margins paid by them and the shares held by them, Business Standard said.</p>
<p>The paper said the defaults pertain to 24/96-97 of the A+B1 group of shares and settlements 12 and 13 of the B2 group of shares.</p>
<p>Exchange officials were not immediately available for confirmation.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
